test_command=sh tests/invocations_test.sh
id=invocations-01 result=green reason=invocations-01: the source prompt runs discover/ensure/state/release and the skills derivation as one-line path invocations of __ANTZ_SCRIPTS_DIR__ (state still carries the probe's path), no temp-file instruction and no include marker survives
id=invocations-02 result=green reason=invocations-02: inject_includes(), its orchestrator-keyed call site and the antz-skills.sh done-carve-out are gone from install.sh, which substitutes the once-resolved libdir for the placeholder at render time; the retired mechanism's no-survivor and fail-loud clauses re-appear render-side in invocations-03/07 and in the surviving libdirinstall-05 atomic-pass suite
id=invocations-03 result=green reason=two tests carry it: invocations-03: both rendered orchestrator bodies are exactly the source prompt with the concrete resolved path substituted -- zero script lines, zero markers, zero placeholders anywhere installed -- with the Claude and OpenCode frontmatter shapes intact; and invocations-03: with XDG_CONFIG_HOME set the invocation lines carry that XDG-resolved concrete path (never the HOME fallback, never a trailing slash)
id=invocations-04 result=green reason=two tests carry it: invocations-04: the rendered body instructs zero re-materialization (no temp file anywhere; every installed-file run is a one-line sh call), the 'Never writes anything itself' Owns bullet holds; and invocations-04: the scripts' machine-line vocabulary is byte-identical -- every pinned literal present in the byte-unchanged scripts/orchestration/ files, historical sh <tempfile> header wording included; verified end-to-end once by the real sh <libdir>/antz-flow.sh state <slug> <libdir>/antz-probe.sh run emitting the probe's subspec= lines
id=invocations-05 result=green reason=invocations-05: the four tables, step 3 classification, step 4 rejection routing, the session guards, the Report Format, the byte-pinned delegation header and the human follow-up print survive both renders; the flow script keeps exactly its four subcommands
id=invocations-06 result=green reason=invocations-06: the source prompt's structural pins of the de-embedded shape -- 4 fenced blocks (8 fence lines, no ```sh), the four tables, steps ending at 6, no new fenced block; the flow-09/orchprose-01 fence-count clause re-scopes itself in sub-spec 05
id=invocations-07 result=green reason=two tests carry it: invocations-07: renders are deterministic and idempotent (two fresh-HOME installs and a same-HOME re-install give byte-identical trees), the body carries no per-session data with the frontmatter marker as its only version-bearing string, and no script line appears in any rendered agent body; and invocations-07: the expected cache effect (KV-cache priority, ~335 embedded lines gone, per-session re-materialization dropping to zero) is recorded in the change README; the CHANGELOG half of that clause is an explicit skip stub (sub-spec 06's declared artifact)
id=invocations-08 result=green reason=two tests carry it: invocations-08: the rendered skills bullets run the installed antz-skills.sh by resolved path with never-a-temp-file-copy, the no-CLI/hook/plugin clause, the byte-unchanged block shapes and the never-read constraint; and invocations-08: the installed antz-skills.sh keeps the derivation output contract untouched -- skill=/path=/matched= lines, cap of five with the alphabetical-by-name tie-break, case-insensitive matching, 'Skills: none matched' at exit 0
